<http://data.silknow.org/object/75d3b673-0f82-3968-a253-b53e15ea2952>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile of brocaded silk in coloured silks, probably designed by John Vansommer, Spitalfields, London, 1730-1769"@en , "Textile of brocaded silk. Cream-white ground brocaded in coloured silks with a design showing mixed clusters of flowers in baskets and cornucopias. Between the chief motifs is a small spray of carnations tied together with a ribbon. There is only one repeat in the width of the textile. There are narrow selvedges woven in tabby with two green and two white woven stripes."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/72a61582-2205-3e4b-87aa-176e57fcc737> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c69c0300-df97-35de-b9b0-e9a7881be180> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/8fe8e9a7-331c-344b-8dda-60f2715628c6> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile of brocaded silk. Cream-white ground brocaded in coloured silks with a design showing mixed clusters of flowers in baskets and cornucopias. Between the chief motifs is a small spray of carnations tied together with a ribbon. There is only one repeat in the width of the textile. There are narrow selvedges woven in tabby with two green and two white woven stripes."@en , "Textile of brocaded silk in coloured silks, probably designed by John Vansommer, Spitalfields, London, 1730-1769"@en ;
